      <article class="project">
        <div class="text">
          <div class="ph"><h3>Sage 100 ERP implementation</h3><span class="when">2024 – 2025</span></div>
          <p class="outcome">Manufacturing, inventory and purchasing on one system; operating cost down 12%.</p>
          <p class="body">Led the rollout across manufacturing operations: mapped how the shop actually works (kits, bins, sales orders, project codes) into ERP workflows, then ran training and adoption for supply-chain, warehouse and manufacturing staff. Combined with Lean workflow changes, this took 12% out of operating cost.</p>
          <ul class="points"><li>Modular training programme covering navigation, purchasing, warehouse, manufacturing and reporting</li><li>Standardized item and BOM upload templates; Sage is now the data source behind the tracking tools above</li></ul>
          <p class="tools"><span>Tools</span>Sage 100 · process mapping · training design</p>
        </div>
        
      </article>
      <article class="project has-media">
        <div class="text">
          <div class="ph"><h3>Manufacturing floor efficiency (DMAIC)</h3><span class="when">2022 – 2023</span></div>
          <p class="outcome">Three lanes built in 162 man-hours instead of 285; $129K saved over the programme.</p>
          <p class="body">The plan called for one platform a week; the floor was two months behind. Fishbone analysis found the causes: an undocumented, person-dependent kit process, no weekly schedule, stale work instructions, disordered picklists. Each got a mistake-proof fix: flowcharts and a master build document, weekly targets, a two-week instruction refresh, reorganized inventory.</p>
          <ul class="points"><li>Main modules: 285 → 162.5 man-hours per three lanes (−43%)</li><li>Kits: 115 → 53 man-hours (−54%)</li></ul>
          <p class="tools"><span>Tools</span>Lean Six Sigma · DMAIC · root cause analysis · Poka-Yoke · production planning</p>
        </div>
        <figure class="media"><img src="data:image/svg+xml;base64," alt="Manufacturing floor efficiency (DMAIC)"></figure>
