      </article>
      
      <article class="project has-media">
        <div class="text">
          <div class="ph"><h3>Digital work instructions and ERP</h3><span class="when">2023 – 2024</span></div>
          <p class="outcome">Assembly time down 11%, assembly defects down 8%.</p>
          <p class="body">Replaced paper assembly instructions for generator sets with animated, step-by-step guides built in Creo Illustrate from the released CAD, with each part highlighted and moved into place in sequence, then implemented the ERP&#x27;s production, BOM and sales-order modules and linked the guides in so assemblers always open the current revision.</p>
          <ul class="points"><li>Shorter learning curve for new assemblers and consistent training across shifts</li><li>Instructions stay in step with design changes because they come from the same models</li></ul>
          <p class="tools"><span>Tools</span>PTC Creo Illustrate · ERP implementation · work-instruction design</p>
